## FINANCIAL RISK MANAGEMENT (continued)
(c) Currency risk
* * *
Currency risk (also referred to as exchange rate risk) refers to the risk arising from adverse fluctuations in exchange rates and gold prices in the market when the Group holds foreign currency positions, including gold. The Group was established and operates in Vietnam and the accounting currency is VND. Major transactions of the Group are also in VND. The Group’s loans to customers were mainly denominated in VND and USD. However, some other assets of the Group are denominated in foreign currencies other than USD. The Group sets limits on the level of exposure by each currency, including gold.

--- https://acb.com.vn/en/investors/financial-statements ---
The currency position is monitored daily and the Group takes risk mitigation actions to ensure that the currency position is within the set limit.
