NOTES 1. The fees specified in the fee schedule do not include value -added tax (VAT). When collecting service fees, Vietcombank will calculate and collect VAT in accordance with current laws. 2. For the fee rate specified in the percentage, the fee collected shall be calculated at the rate of % x corresponding transaction value. 3. The fees specified in the fee schedule do not include fees ( telegraphic transfer, postage, taxes, service fees, etc.) payable to other units and/or banks participating in the provision of services. Vietcombank will collect these fees (if incurred) along with the corresponding Service Fee according to Vietcombank's Fee Schedule. 4. Transactions involving the use of foreign currencies comply with the state's current foreign exchange management regulations. 5. When collecting fees for transferring transactions, in addition to the fee for deducting the transfer account, VCB will collect an additional transfer fee within 2 days from the date the account holder/person authorized by the account holder deposits cash into the account if the source of the transfer is the source of cash deposited into the account within 2 days (if any). 6. When collecting fees for outbound cash deposit transactions, in addition to the outbound cash deposit fee, VCB will collect an additional fee for small VND cash deposit if the deposit amount has a face value of VND 20,000 or less in large quantities (over 100 sheets). 7. Customers can pay the service fee in VND for fees collected in foreign currency at the exchange rate announced by Vietcombank at the time of fee collection. 8. In case individual customers deposit cash into their accounts at Vietcombank, the fee schedule applied to calculate fees is based on the type of credit account, specifically: – In the case individual customer A deposits money into individual customer B's account: the transaction fee is calculated according to the service fee schedule applicable to individual customers; – In case individual customer A deposits money into the account of company C: the transaction fee is calculated according to the fee schedule applicable to customers being organizations and enterprises;
