Vietnam’s economy expanded 8.02% in 
real terms in 2025, retaining its position 
as one of the fastest growing in Asia.  
Despite a challenging environment, 
including increasing global economic 
fragmentation and US trade tariffs, severe 
flooding in northern and central regions, 
and pressure on foreign exchange rates, 
the economy showed its resilience and 
maintained a strong growth trajectory.  
Following the favourable outcome of 
discussions with the US on tariff rates, 
exports continued to expand, domestic 
consumption remained robust, and foreign 
direct investment inflows continued 
to rise. The government continued to 
support economic activity through public 
investment and, importantly, introduced 
four key resolutions aimed at restructuring 
the economy and creating a more 
enabling environment for private sector 
growth. Together, these developments 
have reinforced the foundations for 
Vietnam’s sustainable economic growth in 
the years ahead.
Proven foundations, resilient growth
Supported by Vietnam’s economic 
momentum, underpinned by the 
transformation achieved over the past 
five years, and driven by disciplined 
execution, Techcombank delivered 
another year of robust financial 
performance in 2025.
Total operating income grew by 13.6% year 
on year (Y o Y), while profit before tax reached 
a record VND 32.5 trillion, representing 
an increase of 18.2% Y o Y and beating our 
AGM target. Our return on assets remained 
steady at 2.4%, still among the highest in the 
industry. We achieved these results while 
maintaining our disciplined approach to risk 
management and ensuring strong capital 
adequacy and asset quality. 
Our strong financial performance was driven 
by robust growth in net interest income (NII) 
and net fee income (NFI) and the expansion of 
our wealth business. Our net interest income 
grew by 7.5% Y o Y, supported by strong credit 
demand from retail and corporate customers 
and our effective mitigation of rising funding 
costs amid a competitive liquidity environment. 
We continued to generate more fee income 
than any other Vietnamese bank, with NFI 
up 7.8% Y o Y. This was driven by strong 
momentum in bancassurance fees, which 
grew by 91.8% Y o Y following the launch of 
our general and life insurance businesses, 
together with growth in investment banking 
and FX fees and the expansion of our wealth 
management proposition.
The growth of our credit book once again 
outpaced the industry, expanding over 18% 
in-line with the credit quota granted by the 
SBV. At the same time, our prudent risk 
management kept asset quality high, with 
our non-performing loan ratio remaining 
among the industry’s lowest at 1.13%, while 
our coverage ratio increased to 127.9% 
reflecting the bank’s strong balance sheet.
Supported by robust domestic consumption 
we continued to diversify our credit book 
towards retail and small and medium-sized 
enterprises (SMEs). Our retail book grew 
by 30.8% in 2025, significantly higher than 
the 13.4% growth of our corporate portfolio, 
driven by strong momentum in mortgages 
and higher-yield unsecured lending, margin 
lending and merchant products. 
Within our corporate book we continued 
to strategically diversify lending towards 
economic sectors driven by domestic 
consumption, with real estate reducing to 
31% of our total credit book, down from 33% 
at the end of 2024. 
