Building sustainably
In 2025, Techcombank continued 
to place sustainability at the heart 
of our business strategy and 
operations, guided by the belief 
that sustainable growth is good 
for our customers, shareholders 
and for Vietnam. 
We remained committed to supporting 
corporate clients in advancing green 
development initiatives and adopting more 
sustainable business practices. Leveraging 
our proven capabilities in project financing, 
we expanded our green lending portfolio 
for sustainability-related projects to more 
than VND 18.7 trillion. 
Our retail sustainability offerings continued 
to receive a very positive response. By 
year end we had issued more than 1 million 
Techcombank Visa Eco Debit and Credit 
Cards to customers enabling them to track 
and offset carbon emissions linked to their 
spending. Together, the Techcombank Visa 
Eco Debit and Credit Cards helped to offset 
approximately 201.9 tonnes of CO₂ during 
the year.
Techcombank continued to improve 
our operational efficiency, reducing our 
energy and water consumption despite the 
expansion of our branch network. In fact, we 
were the first Bank in Vietnam to open fully 
paperless branches, further embedding 
sustainability into our operations.  
Our commitment to making a positive 
contribution to society remained strong. 
The 4th Techcombank Hanoi Marathon 
and the 9th Ho Chi Minh City International 
Marathon together attracted a record 
36,000 runners, reinforcing our efforts to 
promote healthy and active lifestyles. Our 
‘Winter Giving’ initiative saw nearly 9,000 
employees and their family members come 
together to plant over 40,000 trees across 
the country. In parallel, Techcombank 
contributed VND 231 billion to support 
social initiatives across Vietnam. 
Recognizing Techcombank’s efforts in 
implementing Environmental, Social, and 
Governance (ESG) principles, advancing 
green finance, and strengthening social 
responsibility, the Ho Chi Minh City Stock 
Exchange included Techcombank in 
the Vietnam Sustainability Index (VNSI), 
placing the Bank among the top 20 listed 
companies with strongest sustainability 
practices in the market.
As the core of a leading integrated financial ecosystem, Techcombank is well positioned 
to capture the new opportunities created by Vietnam’s fast-growing economy and play 
a leading role in enabling and shaping Vietnam’s next phase of development. 
Rising affluence and domestic consumption, coupled to the relative under penetration 
of our core mortgage, wealth, investment and insurance products still provide a 
substantial runway for growth. At the same time, the enhanced regulatory environment 
will open new opportunities for the banking sector, and specifically for Techcombank, 
in areas such as infrastructure and industrial financing, and the development of new 
financial assets – in line with Vietnam's progressive opening to digital assets.
Over the next five years, we are committed to seizing these opportunities, building 
on our position as a national leader to become an integrated financial institution with 
genuine global stature. To achieve this, we have set ourselves bold aspirations to 
double the number of customers we serve, double our market share and increase our 
TOI and PBT fourfold by the end of 2030.
2026 - 2030 Strategy
Vietnam has set a clear ambition to become a high-income, innovation-driven economy 
by 2045. To achieve this goal, the government has passed a series of resolutions (57, 59, 
66 and 68) aimed at accelerating digital transformation, deepening Vietnam’s integration 
into global supply chains, and creating a more enabling environment for the private 
sector to emerge as the primary engine of growth.
Together, these reforms are expected to drive a major restructuring of Vietnam’s 
economic model. Their successful implementation will require substantial capital 
formation to finance large-scale investments in physical and digital infrastructure, support 
the transition towards advanced, higher value-added manufacturing, and to promote 
development that is green and sustainable. 
Against this backdrop, Techcombank and 
Vietnam stand together at the beginning of
 new era of high growth.
