features. We migrated eight applications 
from the traditional data warehouse to 
the lake platform, consolidating pipelines, 
improving latency, and reducing total cost 
of ownership.
• At the heart of our model development is an 
Enterprise Feature Store containing ~12,500 
reusable features—from behavioral signals 
to merchant attributes and risk indicators. 
This shared asset library dramatically reduces 
time-to-model, enforces governance, and 
increases consistency across use cases.
• Our Artificial intelligence/ Machine Learning 
Operations (AI/ML Ops) — Continuous 
Integration/Continuous Delivery (CI/CD) 
for models, automated retraining, model 
monitoring, and lineage—are supplemented 
by AI copilots and agents that accelerate 
code generation and operational automation.
These investments ensure that AI products are not one-off pilots but reliable services 
continuously learning from fresh data.
FUELING PRODUCT  
GROWTH AND  
CREDIT EXPANSION
AI is a key driver of our lending growth.
• In Unsecured Lending, we now run 
AI-powered underwriting that blends 
merchant identification, sales turnover 
estimation, and image analytics to enrich 
applications and detect anomalies.
• In Merchant Lending, partnerships and 
advanced credit models have expanded 
reach and improved unit economics. This 
has supported lending of above VND 
6 Trillion, while improving risk selection 
and customer experience.
• Our Next Best Offer (NBO) capability 
now covers six products, achieving 176–
234% Conversion Rate (CR) uplift, which 
translates into higher cross-sell and deeper 
primary relationships. 
• Altogether, DnA initiatives enabled ~6.2 
trillion VND in lending and helped the 
Bank develop Vietnam’s first ROMI (Return 
on Marketing Investment) model for any 
industry — an enduring advantage that 
connects marketing spend to financial 
outcomes with precision.
