8.6 million, reinforcing Techcombank’s 
leadership position in Vietnam’s digital 
banking landscape and demonstrating 
readiness to compete at regional standards.
Relationship-led banking continued to be 
a distinctive pillar of Techcombank’s digital 
banking in 2025 through the expansion 
of Family and Friend Banking. The Family 
Chapter proposition was enhanced to 
deepen engagement and deposit stickiness, 
particularly through CASA balances. New 
security and support tools were introduced 
to improve transparency and peace of mind 
for family members, while push notifications 
strengthened real-time communication. 
By the end of 2025, the number of active 
family groups reached approximately 
46,000, contributing an incremental VND 
82,812 billion in total AUM. Customers 
participating in family-linked relationships 
demonstrated engagement levels 64% 
higher than individual users, underscoring 
the effectiveness of this approach in 
increasing customer lifetime value.
Friend Banking was further elevated 
through its integration with Auto-earning 
Plus, delivering a differentiated market 
proposition. A redesigned onboarding 
journey with full configuration options 
enabled customers to form and manage 
groups intuitively, supported by a 
centralized dashboard and member-
