Engineering Excellence
DRIVING PRODUCTIVITY 
THROUGH AI ADOPTION AND 
ENGINEERING DISCIPLINE
Software productivity improved significantly 
by integrating AI-assisted development with 
stricter quality controls. Amazon Q, an AI tool 
designed to assist developers in writing and 
reviewing code, was implemented across 
engineering teams. By the end of the year, 
75-80% of developers were using Amazon 
Q on a weekly basis, resulting in an average 
increase of approximately 700 additional 
lines of code per developer each week. 
This enhancement in delivery capacity was 
achieved without increasing the workforce.
These productivity gains were further 
supported by enhancing the reuse of 
existing software services, which reduced 
the need to recreate similar functions 
across different systems. The service 
reusability rate reached 50%, surpassing 
the annual target of 35% by over 40%. 
Additionally, the amount of duplicated 
code detected during scanning decreased 
to 77.7%, significantly outperforming the 
targeted reduction of 50%.
In terms of quality, increased automation 
facilitated earlier detection of defects in the 
software development lifecycle. Automated 
functional testing reached 83.8%, 
exceeding the target of 78%. Moreover, 
defect leakage into User Acceptance 
Testing (UAT) was reduced by 57.9%, nearly 
doubling the planned improvement. This 
led to enhanced release stability and a 
decrease in operational risk.
INNOVATION
GenAI Platform
(Enterprise-grade
AI foundation)
Intelligence Hub
(Safe access to 
leading AI tools)
AE+ Chatbot
(Frontline product 
enablement)
Techcombank accelerated innovation 
by operationalizing AI in a controlled, 
bank-grade environment focusing on 
measurable productivity gains, faster 
frontline enablement, and stronger 
decision support.
The Bank continued to mature its GenAI 
Platform and delivered the Business 
Analyst Agent, which reduced manual 
effort by ~70% in key business analysis 
tasks. Building on this, 2026 roadmap 
expands to additional agents across the 
delivery lifecycle (e.g., architecture and 
solution design assistance, tester support, 
and software development). The long-
term vision is a “virtual development 
team”, a set of specialized AI agents that 
amplify engineering throughput by multiple 
times while improving accuracy through 
connected data inputs, enabling faster and 
more reliable analysis and decision-making.
IT also launched the Intelligence Hub, 
providing employees with access 
to leading AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, 
DeepSeek, Claude, etc.) within a secure, 
governed banking environment designed 
to prevent data leakage and protect 
confidential information.
To strengthen frontline advisory 
effectiveness, IT implemented the AE+ 
chatbot with 200+ curated Q&A items 
drawn from AE+ product knowledge. This 
capability helps reduce response time by 
approximately 94% when frontline teams 
need quick, consistent answers while 
consulting customers, improving both 
service speed and customer experience 
at branches.
CYBERSECURITY Cybersecurity is essential for 
Techcombank. As one of the largest banks 
in Vietnam, Techcombank operates on a 
large scale and is a primary target for cyber 
threats in the industry. Despite a highly 
complex threat landscape, the Bank is 
committed to maintaining its position while 
ensuring business continuity, customer 
trust, and regulatory compliance. This 
is achieved through a specialized and 
skilled information security team, bolstered 
by strong engineering capabilities and 
advanced automation.
Key cyber security 
achievements in 2025
142,548 security events detected and 
handled (+5.3% Y o Y), with zero impact 
on system availability, including 57,371 
medium-risk and 41,143 high-risk 
attack attempts;
Identified and resolved 28,423 leaked 
credentials and sensitive customer data 
exposed on the internet (2x vs. 2024);
Discovered and remediated 5 critical 
vulnerabilities on AWS infrastructure, 
preventing potential large-scale data 
leakage and material financial and 
reputational risks;
Detected and mitigated 2,642 
fraudulent websites, applications, social 
media pages, and phishing messages 
impersonating Techcombank;
Automated analysis of 37,429 new 
Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures 
(CVEs), reducing detection and response 
time for high and critical vulnerabilities to 
4.34 hours (38% Y o Y faster);
Completed vulnerability assessment 
across 100% of Techcombank assets 
(27,468 assets), to proactively fix and 
prevent exploitation;
Established standardized AI security 
controls, enabling safe and scalable 
deployment of multiple AI agents 
across the Bank.
Built and deployed in-house security 
tools (Red Team Hunter, AI threat 
modeling, firewall audit, configuration 
verification), improving protection 
efficiency while reducing external 
license costs;
