SYSTEM OPERATION 
AND UPGRADES Operation Excellence
OPTIMIZATION
IT OPERATIONAL RISKS 
AND COMPLIANCE
Optimization is a core pillar of operational excellence, enabling the Bank to scale efficiently, 
control costs, and improve performance without compromising service quality or resilience.
Operational risk and compliance 
governance have been reinforced through 
disciplined execution and strict adherence 
to regulatory and internal standards. For 
the second consecutive year, we achieved 
100% timely resolution of IT operational 
risks and compliance findings, resulting in 
no overdue items.
Additionally, IT conducted five internal 
compliance assessments across key 
operational areas and successfully 
managed over ten audit and assessment 
programs involving both internal 
stakeholders and external organizations, 
such as ISO and PCI DSS.
Cloud Cost Optimization
Notification Hub
IT improved cloud efficiency by increasing 
the adoption of AWS Graviton processors, 
which are AWS-designed chips that offer 
better price-performance. The usage of 
Graviton-based EC2 instances, Amazon's 
cloud computing service for running 
applications and workloads, rose from 5% 
to 20%. This shift resulted in securing USD 
500,000 in AWS credits. 
In combination with capacity right-sizing, 
reserved instance planning, and storage 
lifecycle optimization, these efforts 
produced annual cloud cost savings of 
USD 3.2 million and achieved a Cloud 
Optimization score of 70.64%. This score 
surpasses that of regional high-performing 
banks, which average around 50%.
The centralized Notification Hub delivered near real-time transaction alerts ( ~1 second), 
integrated 39 services, and generated cumulative savings of approximately VND 80 
Billion (2023 – 2025).
Database 
optimization & archive
We implemented a structured database 
archiving program to optimize data storage 
and system performance. A total of 126 
production databases were archived, which 
reduced the data volume in live systems 
and improved processing efficiency. This 
initiative decreased the infrastructure load, 
enhanced system stability, and lowered 
both long-term storage and operating costs. 
Additionally, we ensured that historical data 
remained accessible while complying with 
regulatory and audit requirements.
