HISTORY OF 
ESTABLISHMENT AND 
DEVELOPMENT 
Established Foreign Exchange 
Bureau under National Bank 
of Vietnam – predecessor of 
Vietcombank
On April 1st, 1963  Officially 
put into operation (According 
to Decree No 115/CP dated 
October 30th 1962 of the 
Government)
From April 1965 to April 1975, 
directly involved in operating the 
monetary route (code-named 
B29), receiving and “processing” 
foreign currency, to support and 
fund the revolution in the South.
From April 1975 to 1987, took over the 
oldexisting banking system, inheriteding 
Vietnam’s membership rights in international 
financial organisations, participated in 
handling played a key role in managing 
national debts, combating embargoes, and 
successfully assumed the role as the sole 
bank with monopoly rights in three key areas: 
foreign exchange, import-export credit, and 
international transaction settlements
BeingAs the sole commercial 
bank authorised to issue 
Vietnamese Dong-denominated 
foreign currency bonds, 
Vietcombank played a crucial role 
in implementing synchronized 
management for the use and 
expenditure of foreign currencies.
From 2000 – 2005, 
Vietcombank pioneered building 
and successfully implemented 
Banking Restructuring and 
Modernisation Project.
On June 2, 2008, Vietcombank 
was officially converted into a 
joint-stock commercial bank after 
pioneering its initial public offering 
(IPO) and successfully issuing 
shares to the public in 2007.
On June 30, 2009, 
Vietcombank’s shares (stock 
code: VCB) were officially listed 
and traded on the Ho Chi Minh 
City Stock Exchange (HOSE)
On September 30, 2011, 
Vietcombank signed a strategic 
shareholder agreement with 
Mizuho Corporate Bank, a part 
of the Mizuho Financial Group 
from Japan.
On March 31st 2013, 
Vietcombank launched a new 
brand identity system and slogan 
“Together for the future”
On December 1, 2016, 
Vietcombank issued its 
development strategy until 2020. 
In the same year, Vietcombank 
regained the number one position 
in terms of profit.
On October 19, 2018, Vietcombank 
inaugurated its operations in Laos.
On November 28, 2018, Vietcombank 
became the first bank officially approved by 
the State Bank of Vietnam with Decision 
No. 2315/QD-NHNN to apply Basel II 
under Circular 41 from January 1, 2019, one 
year ahead of the prescribed deadline.
On November 1, 2019, Vietcombank 
inaugurated its representative office 
in the United States. It became the 
first Vietnamese bank to achieve a 
profit milestone of 1 billion USD. On 
November 12, 2019, Vietcombank 
signed a distribution agreement with 
FWD Insurance Company, the largest 
in terms of life insurance at the time 
of signing.
On January 27, 2020, Vietcombank 
successfully launched its Core 
Banking system   
From 2020 to 2023, steadfastly 
overcoming the Covid-19 
pandemic, Vietcombank has 
solidified its position as the 
number one bank in Vietnam 
across multiple fronts and among 
the top 100 largest listed banks 
globally by market apitalization, 
according to Reuters.
