Assessment of the Board of Directors 
on the activities of the Board of Management 
Orientation of the Board of Directors’ activities 
in 2026
In 2026, the global economy is forecast to face many 
potential difficulties and challenges arising from geopolitical 
competition, trade protectionism, supply chain disruptions, 
technological races, and especially the restructuring of the 
global order. For Vietnam, 2026 has particularly important 
significance as the first year of implementing the 2026–2030 
Five-Year Socio-Economic Development Plan, marking the 
beginning of a new development era with a GDP growth 
target of 10% or higher, setting unprecedented requirements 
for reforms and improvements in institutional quality, focusing 
on strongly enhancing national competitiveness and creating 
an attractive environment for investors and businesses. 
The State Bank of Vietnam is expected to continue flexibly 
operating policy instruments to control inflation, stabilize 
exchange rates, and promote capital supply to the economy; 
at the same time, strengthening system soundness, ensuring 
safety, and creating favorable conditions for credit institutions 
to develop.
With the determination to build BIDV into a LARGE – STRONG – 
GREEN Financial-Banking Group in Southeast Asia; thoroughly 
implementing the Government’s policies and the SBV’s 
directions, and based on the 2026 business plan orientation of 
the entire BIDV system, the Board of Directors will continue to 
fully perform its functions and duties in accordance with legal 
regulations and BIDV’s internal rules, resolutely addressing 
existing limitations and leading the entire system to focus on 
implementing the following key tasks in 2026:
The Board of Directors (BOD) conducted a comprehensive and 
thorough assessment of the Board of Management’s activities 
through reports on business performance and issues discussed 
at BOD meetings, specialized working programs by sector, and 
close supervision through the activities of the BOD’s committees 
and advisory and supporting units. In 2025, the operations of the 
Board of Management were continuously improved, enhancing 
effectiveness and efficiency, moving toward advanced practices 
and high standards in the market. The Board of Management, 
led by the Chief Executive Officer, operates business operation, 
promoting collective intelligence and the single-leader regime 
to ensure the proper, full, and effective implementation 
of Resolutions and Decisions of the General Meeting of 
Shareholders and the Board of Directors, as well as compliance 
with legal regulations.
Some notable operational results of the Board of Management 
in 2025 are as follows:
  • Based on the overall business plan orientation of the entire 
system, the Chief Executive Officer directed units to urgently 
develop and issue Action Program No. 1500/CTr-BIDV, assigning 
tasks to each member of the Board of Management and 
specialized units, ensuring clarity of responsibilities, tasks, 
accountability, timelines, and outcomes.
  •  In 2025, the Chief Executive Officer directed the review and re-
issuance of Decision No. 6922/QĐ-BIDV dated August 28, 2025 
on the assignment of duties among members of the Board of 
Management; promoting the capacity, experiences, roles and 
responsibilities of each individual and strengthening coordination 
and communication among the Board of Management members 
and between the Board of Management members and BOD 
members in the same assigned fields; contributing to innovation 
and enhancement of governance and executive capacity, as well 
as high-level direction, inspection, and supervision by key leaders 
at BIDV in particular and the operational efficiency of the BIDV 
system in general.
  • In 2025, the Board of Management focused on leading, directing, 
and managing key and priority issues of the BIDV system, achieving 
many positive and outstanding results: growth in total assets, 
credit, and mobilization, continuing to rank first in the market 
in operational scale for many consecutive years; operational 
efficiency and structure improved sustainably amid increasingly 
intense market competition; asset quality well controlled, with 
credit risk management emphasized, helping maintain the credit 
portfolio within safe limits; flexible implementation of solutions 
to ensure liquidity safety and compliance with regulatory safety 
ratios; improved capital utilization efficiency and cost control, 
optimizing asset and capital structure to enhance profitability; 
continued acceleration of digital transformation, strengthening 
technological mastery and expanding the application of new 
scientific and technological achievements such as AI, Big 
Data, etc. across most areas of operation; development of 
human resources and working environment, ensuring income 
and employment for employees at a highly competitive level 
compared to the market; operations of BIDV’s presences in Laos, 
Cambodia, and Myanmar continued to be emphasized and 
enhanced, making effective and practical contributions to the 
implementation of the Vietnamese Government’s foreign policy 
on developing economic, political, and diplomatic relations with 
countries in the region;...
The Board of Directors acknowledges and highly appreciates 
the efforts and operational results of the Chief Executive Officer 
and members of the Board of Management in 2025; continuing 
to maintain solidarity and high unity, promoting collective 
intelligence, responsibility, exemplary conduct, innovation, and 
creativity; contributing to enhancing BIDV’s image, reputation, 
position, and brand in the market, achieving and exceeding 
the business targets and plans assigned by the SBV, the 
General Meeting of Shareholders, and the Board of Directors, 
thereby creating strong and sustainable momentum for BIDV’s 
breakthrough development in the coming period.
Decisively implement plans to increase charter capital and own capital to enhance financial capacity and 
improve the CAR ratio. Increase capital mobilization from the beginning of the year, focusing on improving 
the ratio of low-cost demand deposits in an effective and sustainable manner.1
Promote customer base development, prioritizing potential customer segments (small and medium-sized 
enterprises, foreign-invested enterprises, retail customers, and customers on digital channels); improve the 
ratio of active customers and the product/service usage per customer.2
Effectively fulfill the role of capital supplier to the economy, with credit capital focusing on priority sectors and 
growth drivers in line with the Government’s and SBV’s orientations; at the same time, strictly control credit 
quality and accelerate the recovery and resolution of bad debts, potential debts, and off-balance-sheet debts.3
Comprehensively transform BIDV’s operations from the credit model and business model in line with new trends, 
suitable to the characteristics of the Vietnamese market and international banking best practices. Streamline 
processes, regulations, and workflows in association with reviewing the functions and duties of units.4
Strengthen innovation and extensive application of technology. Encourage a culture of daring to think and 
daring to act to improve labor productivity, optimize costs, and deliver superior customer experiences.5
Manage finance effectively, optimize the CIR ratio; enhance governance and executive capacity at all levels; 
consolidate and improve personnel quality toward restructuring resources, increasing the proportion of 
frontline business staff and “digital” personnel; practice a risk control culture and cultivate corporate cultural 
values, thereby providing strong support for business operations.
