2024 BIDV also developed modern digital banking platforms, 
expanded its digital ecosystem, and enhanced customer 
experience (including SmartBanking for individuals and Bank 
Direct for corporates). These achievements marked a new 
milestone in digital transformation, strengthening BIDV’s 
operational capabilities and competitiveness in the digital era.
Enhancing capital efficiency and cost control:
The Board of Management focused on optimizing the structure 
of assets and funding sources to improve profitability. A closed 
loop financial management model was developed, ensuring 
seamless connectivity from Head Office to branches, thereby 
enhancing efficient and safe capital utilization alongside cost 
optimization measures. In 2025, BIDV completed a charter 
capital increase transaction through private placement 
to five institutional investors with a total issuance value of 
VND4,805 billion, including an increase of VND1,238 billion 
in charter capital and VND3,566 billion in share premium. In 
2025, BIDV was honored as “Enterprise with outstanding M&A 
deals for 2024–2025” . Owners’ equity reached VND163,017 
billion (up 19.6%), helping improve the capital adequacy ratio 
(CAR) to 9%. Profitability and operational safety indicators 
were maintained, while liquidity ratios and the ratio of short 
term funds used for medium and long term lending were all in 
compliance with regulatory requirements.
Human resource development and working environment:
The bank implemented a KPI evaluation framework and 
categorized staff based on performance, closely linking results 
with rewards and disciplinary measures. Training content and 
methods were innovated in line with best practices, fostering a 
culture of continuous learning and innovation, and enhancing 
workforce capabilities to meet development requirements in 
the new phase.
Overall, BIDV’s management in 2025 achieved positive results 
across multiple aspects. The bank timely implemented new 
governance solutions and organizational restructuring, 
thereby improving operational efficiency across the system. 
Improvements in structure, policies, technology, and human 
resources created substantive enhancements in governance 
capability, making an important contribution to the successful 
achievement of BIDV’s 2025 objectives.
Management results in 2025
Implementing ESG initiatives
In 2025, the Board of Management of BIDV implemented 
numerous management innovations, contributing to 
enhancing efficiency across the bank’s system.
Restructuring the organization toward a streamlined and 
modern model:
BIDV completed its organizational model in line with a modern 
commercial bank, meeting international practices. In the year, 
the bank reorganized the operating model at head office and 
branch network by consolidating the operating models of 
16 branches, terminating operations of 7 underperforming 
transaction offices, and transferring 55 transaction offices 
among branches to optimize the network. At the same 
time, BIDV standardized hundreds of internal processes 
and regulations to simplify procedures and improve labor 
productivity. 
Accelerating comprehensive, synchronized, structured, 
and substantive transformation across all areas of 
operation:
Focusing resources on continuing the implementation of the 
retail banking operating model transformation; expanding and 
developing the digital banking ecosystem while enhancing 
digital experience for corporate customers; deploying a 
centralized and integrated risk management model; building 
a closed loop and end to end financial management model 
to improve advisory effectiveness and ensure system safety 
and efficiency; proactively exploring and implementing 
investment activities in new sectors; and strengthening digital 
2 3
BIDV consistently upheld Environmental, Social and 
Governance (ESG) criteria in its operations, aiming for 
sustainable development and harmonizing interests with the 
community. The bank has actively financed environmentally 
friendly projects, providing green credit to nearly 2,000 
projects nationwide with outstanding loans exceeding 
VND82,300 billion - the largest in the market. BIDV’s green 
credit portfolio focused on renewable energy, clean agriculture 
and carbon emission reduction projects, accounting for more 
than 10.8% of total outstanding green credit in the economy. In 
addition, BIDV implemented various green financing product 
initiatives, including Green Deposits, issuance of sustainable 
bonds and expanded advisory services for corporate green 
bond issuance. Internally, the bank promoted a paperless 
office model and digitalized processes to reduce paper and 
energy consumption, thereby minimizing the environmental 
impact of its operations. BIDV also actively participated 
in afforestation and environmental protection programs. 
Notably, between 2024–2025, the bank funded the planting of 
an additional 160,000 trees in various localities, contributing 
to ecological improvement and climate change response.
transformation, IT application, and innovation to enhance 
governance and operational efficiency.
Innovating risk governance and internal control policies:
The bank strengthened its risk governance framework toward 
more advanced standards, strictly complying with regulations 
of the State Bank of Vietnam and aligning with international 
practices. In the year, BIDV implemented a bankwide risk 
identification program and assessed key risks for the 2025–
2028 period, thereby proactively preventing emerging risks. 
Inspection and compliance supervision were enhanced 
through the application of technology for remote monitoring 
and early warning, reinforcing discipline. In addition, the bank 
actively prepared necessary conditions to meet the Basel 3 
roadmap ahead of schedule, moving toward international risk 
management standards.
Comprehensive transformation of retail banking operations:
BIDV successfully implemented a nationwide comprehensive 
transformation of its retail banking operations, fully executing 
standardized designs in line with international consultancy. 
Sales management has undergone a strong shift toward 
professionalization through proper segmentation-based 
management, focusing sales resources on high-value 
customers, and clearly separating sales from credit operations. 
The sales model has transitioned from passive to proactive 
through the application of structured planning processes on 
a daily, weekly, and monthly basis, with staff leveraging new 
support tools such as CRM and Daily Dashboard to enhance 
customer portfolio management and business performance 
management. Staff capabilities and sales mindset have 
also been strengthened through a structured and practical 
training roadmap.
Promoting comprehensive digital transformation in 
management:
Throughout 2025, BIDV accelerated digital transformation 
across all areas of operation, considering it a key lever for 
improving governance effectiveness. The bank focused 
resources on implementing major technology projects, 
with 12 out of 16 key IT projects developed and deployed in 
house. Notably, BIDV successfully mastered and launched 
its new Core Banking Profile system for Y angon Branch (in 
Myanmar) within a record time of 6 months, 7 .5 times faster 
than the partner’s initial timeline, saving 63% of project 
costs. Technology infrastructure, application security and 
