IN 2025 BUSINESS OPERATION MANAGEMENT’S REPORT
Business orientation in 2026
Entering 2026, BIDV sets out a new strategic orientation for the 2026–2030 period with the 
objective of developing the bank to be a “Large – Strong – Green” . The Board of Management 
defines the overarching operating motto for 2026 as “Discipline - Quality - Efficiency - 
Comprehensive Transformation”, with the following key objectives and priorities:
CONTROLLING CREDIT QUALITY , HANDLING NON-PERFORMING AND POTENTIAL 
PROBLEM LOANS
Ensuring that credit growth is aligned with quality and safety without lowering credit standards. Developing and implementing 
plans for handling non-performing and potential problem loans by segment and by branch, with clear roadmaps and specific 
targets. Strengthening post-lending management, monitoring cash flows, and supervising the use of funds to ensure full 
compliance with credit processes and regulations.
STRENGTHENING FINANCIAL CAPACITY AND CAPITAL SAFETY
Aggressively implementing plans to increase charter capital and equity, ensuring improvement in the capital adequacy ratio and 
creating room for medium and long term growth. Proactively developing a roadmap to gradually comply with Basel III standards and 
international governance practices, in conjunction with comprehensive risk management and optimization of capital efficiency.
CONTINUING TO PROMOTE A KEY MARKET LEADING ROLE
Proactively and pioneeringly implementing the policies and 
directions of the Party, the State, and the banking sector, 
contributing to maintaining stability in the monetary and 
banking market, ensuring system safety, and providing 
timely capital for key growth drivers of the economy, thereby 
supporting the realization of double digit economic growth 
targets. Implementing the business development strategy for 
the 2026–2030 period upon approval; developing component 
strategies and organizing execution in close alignment with 
the objectives and solutions of the overall strategy, aiming to 
position BIDV as a “Large - Strong - Green” bank.
ENHANCING BUSINESS EFFICIENCY AND PROFITABILITY
Focusing on restructuring the balance sheet and managing 
interest rates flexibly to improve NIM in a substantive manner, 
optimizing the balance between cost of funds, liquidity, and 
profitability to support overall profit targets. Promoting the 
development of sustainable service income, particularly 
in retail banking, digital banking, insurance, payments, and 
services for FDI customers and value chains. Strengthening 
control over operating and management expenses, promoting 
cost efficiency and anti-waste practices, and developing a 
heatmap of CIR across branches. Enhancing competitiveness 
and operational efficiency of subsidiaries, joint ventures, and 
affiliates.
ENHANCING ORGANIZATIONAL EFFICIENCY AND EXECUTION DISCIPLINE
Reviewing and comprehensively evaluating the effectiveness 
of the streamlined organizational model, clearly defining 
the functions, duties, and responsibilities of each unit 
and position; establishing KPI based mechanisms for task 
assignment, monitoring, and performance evaluation, closely 
linked to personnel management, emulation, rewards, and 
discipline. On that basis, continuing the transformation of 
operations from Head Office to branches in association 
with administrative procedure reform, building a high quality 
and agile workforce capable of meeting transformation 
requirements and enhancing competitiveness in the new 
phase.

